---
/*
  Tolkly's widget, rebuilt from its own source and set where it lives: in the
  corner of somebody else's site.

  The site is Shelf, a shop Tolkly's own landing uses as an example
  (apps/server/src/landing/copy.ts): its colours, its corner radius and the
  question about returns are that example's. The widget is drawn from
  packages/widget/src/styles.ts at its real size — the 380 px window, the
  56 px launcher, the 14/20 type, the 12 px corners a 12 px site gets — and
  scaled as one piece, so its proportions stay the product's. Its accent, font
  and corners are the site's, because that is what the widget does: it reads
  them from the customer's page. The shop is set in Rubik and so is the
  widget; neither is the face of the page around them.

  The words are the widget's own strings (packages/widget/src/i18n.ts, `en`),
  in the order the answer pipeline sends its events: searching, the clauses
  found, the quotes checked, the statement with its source mark, the check
  made visible under it. The second question is one the rules do not cover:
  the refusal says so, keeps the order number from the message, and one press
  hands it to people. The card that lands in the team's Telegram topic is the
  bot's own (apps/server/src/telegram/bot.ts): the project and the reason, the
  order, the page, the question and what the AI did with it.

  The log keeps to its end the way the real one does. Messages grow into it
  from the bottom, and once they outgrow the window the oldest leave over the
  top: the log is a column aligned to its end, with a filler after the last
  message that takes up whatever room is left while there is any. Nothing here
  computes a scroll position.

  Decorative in full, hidden from assistive technology, but for the reload
  button in the bar, which plays the run again: the product's claims are made
  in the prose beside it.
*/
---

<div class="tolkly" data-scene data-dur="10600" data-ease="linear" data-offscreen-pause>
  <div class="browser" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="bar">
      <span class="dots"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>
      <span class="url">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 11V8a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v3M6 11h12v9H6z" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linejoin="round"></path></svg>
        shelf.example
      </span>
      <span class="tag">sample</span>
    </div>

    <div class="site">
      <div class="s-head">
        <span class="s-logo"><i></i>Shelf</span>
        <span class="s-nav"><span>Catalogue</span><span>Delivery</span><span>Returns</span><span>Contacts</span></span>
      </div>
      <p class="s-h">Books and home goods delivered in a day</p>
      <p class="s-p">Free delivery in town from $30.</p>
      <span class="s-cta">To the catalogue</span>
      <div class="s-blocks">
        <span><small>Books</small><b>12,400</b></span>
        <span><small>Home</small><b>3,100</b></span>
        <span><small>Gifts</small><b>860</b></span>
      </div>

      <!-- The widget, at the size the product draws it, scaled as one piece. -->
      <div class="corner">
        <div class="window">
          <div class="head">
            <span class="mono">S</span>
            <span class="who"><b>Shelf</b><span class="status-line">By the site's rules</span></span>
            <span class="x">
              <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6.4 5 5 6.4l5.6 5.6L5 17.6 6.4 19l5.6-5.6 5.6 5.6 1.4-1.4-5.6-5.6L19 6.4 17.6 5 12 10.6z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg>
            </span>
          </div>

          <div class="log">
            <div class="msg bot">
              <span class="ai-tag">AI</span>
              <p class="text">Hello! I am the AI assistant of Shelf. I answer from the delivery and returns rules.</p>
            </div>

            <div class="grow" style="--t: 2.05; --h: 40px">
              <div class="msg user"><span class="bubble">How do I return an item?</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="grow" style="--t: 2.25; --h: 24px">
              <span class="ai-tag">AI</span>
            </div>

            <!-- What the pipeline is doing, from the events it really sends. -->
            <div class="grow status-row" style="--t: 2.25; --h: 24px; --gap: 4px; --out: 4.25">
              <span class="status">
                <span class="st st-search">
                  <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M10.5 17.5a7 7 0 1 1 0-14 7 7 0 0 1 0 14zM15.5 15.5l5 5"></path></svg>
                  Searching the rules of Shelf…
                </span>
                <span class="st st-found">
                  <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 3.5h7l4 4V20a.5.5 0 0 1-.5.5h-10.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5zM14 3.5V8h4M9.5 12h5M9.5 15.5h5"></path></svg>
                  Found 2 clauses
                </span>
                <span class="st st-check">
                  <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3.5l7 2.6v5.4c0 4.4-3 7.8-7 9-4-1.2-7-4.6-7-9V6.1zM8.8 12.2l2.2 2.2 4.3-4.4"></path></svg>
                  Checking the quotes…
                </span>
                <span class="st st-write">Writing on…</span>
              </span>
            </div>

            <div class="grow answer" style="--t: 3.85; --h: 48px; --gap: 4px">
              <p class="para">
                Returns are accepted within 14 days, with the packaging and the receipt.<span class="cite">1</span>
              </p>
            </div>

            <!-- The quote opens right under the claim it backs, as copied, with its link. -->
            <div class="peek">
              <p class="quote">An item of proper quality can be returned within 14 days with its packaging and receipt.</p>
              <span class="peek-link">
                <span class="title">4. Timing</span><i class="sep"></i><span class="from">Returns</span>
                <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M14 5h5v5M19 5l-8.5 8.5M17.5 13.5v4a1.5 1.5 0 0 1-1.5 1.5H6.5A1.5 1.5 0 0 1 5 17.5V8a1.5 1.5 0 0 1 1.5-1.5h4"></path></svg>
              </span>
            </div>

            <div class="grow" style="--t: 4.3; --h: 28px; --gap: 12px">
              <span class="verified">
                <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 3.5l7 2.6v5.4c0 4.4-3 7.8-7 9-4-1.2-7-4.6-7-9V6.1zM8.8 12.2l2.2 2.2 4.3-4.4"></path></svg>
                Checked against the rules: 1 of 1
              </span>
            </div>

            <div class="grow" style="--t: 4.4; --h: 44px; --gap: 12px">
              <div class="after">
                <span class="act">
                  <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7.5 10.5v9h-3v-9zM7.5 10.5l3.6-6.3c.5-.8 1.7-.6 1.9.3l.4 1.8-1 4.2h5.7c1.2 0 2.1 1.1 1.8 2.3l-1.4 5.8c-.2.9-1 1.4-1.8 1.4H7.5"></path></svg>
                  It helped
                </span>
                <span class="act">
                  <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 12a4 4 0 1 0 0-8 4 4 0 0 0 0 8zM4.5 20.5c.8-3.6 3.9-6 7.5-6s6.7 2.4 7.5 6"></path></svg>
                  Talk to an operator
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <div class="grow" style="--t: 7.35; --h: 64px">
              <div class="msg user"><span class="bubble">Can you deliver to a pickup locker? It's for order 48213.</span></div>
            </div>

            <div class="grow" style="--t: 7.55; --h: 24px">
              <span class="ai-tag">AI</span>
            </div>

            <div class="grow status-row" style="--t: 7.55; --h: 24px; --gap: 4px; --out: 8.4">
              <span class="status">
                <span class="st">
                  <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M10.5 17.5a7 7 0 1 1 0-14 7 7 0 0 1 0 14zM15.5 15.5l5 5"></path></svg>
                  Searching the rules of Shelf…
                </span>
              </span>
            </div>

            <!-- Nothing in the rules: said plainly, with the order kept and a way to a person. -->
            <div class="grow" style="--t: 8.4; --h: 200px; --gap: 4px">
              <div class="card refused">
                <p class="refusal">I did not find this in the help pages and rules of the site.</p>
                <span class="tokens">
                  <span class="token">
                    <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 3.5h7l4 4V20a.5.5 0 0 1-.5.5h-10.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5zM14 3.5V8h4M9.5 12h5M9.5 15.5h5"></path></svg>
                    Order 48213
                  </span>
                </span>
                <span class="press">
                  <span class="act primary">
                    <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 12a4 4 0 1 0 0-8 4 4 0 0 0 0 8zM4.5 20.5c.8-3.6 3.9-6 7.5-6s6.7 2.4 7.5 6"></path></svg>
                    Hand over to an operator
                  </span>
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- The press: the button gives way, and the handoff is its own reply. -->
            <div class="grow" style="--t: 9.55; --h: 24px">
              <span class="ai-tag">AI</span>
            </div>

            <div class="grow" style="--t: 9.55; --h: 180px; --gap: 4px">
              <div class="card">
                <p class="refusal">Bringing in an operator.</p>
                <span class="tokens">
                  <span class="token">
                    <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M7 3.5h7l4 4V20a.5.5 0 0 1-.5.5h-10.5a.5.5 0 0 1-.5-.5V4a.5.5 0 0 1 .5-.5zM14 3.5V8h4M9.5 12h5M9.5 15.5h5"></path></svg>
                    Order 48213
                  </span>
                </span>
                <span class="waiting">
                  <span class="waiting-head"><i class="pulse"></i>Waiting for an operator…</span>
                  <span class="waiting-hint">You can add details here: the operator will see them.</span>
                </span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="compose">
            <span class="field">
              <span class="ph ph-ask">Write a question…</span>
              <span class="ph ph-op">Message to the operator…</span>
              <span class="line q1"><span>How do I return an item?</span></span>
              <span class="line q2"><span>Can you deliver to a pickup locker? It's for order 48213.</span></span>
            </span>
            <span class="send">
              <svg class="icon" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 19V5M5.5 11.5 12 5l6.5 6.5"></path></svg>
            </span>
          </div>
          <p class="foot">Powered by Tolkly</p>
        </div>

        <span class="launcher">
          <svg class="icon when-closed" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M5.5 2.5h6A3.5 3.5 0 0 1 15 6v1h-3a5 5 0 0 0-5 5v1H5.5A3.5 3.5 0 0 1 2 9.5V6a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 3.5-3.5zM12 8.5h6.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1 3.5 3.5v3.5a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-3.5 3.5v2.1c0 .6-.7.9-1.2.5L14.6 19H12a3.5 3.5 0 0 1-3.5-3.5V12A3.5 3.5 0 0 1 12 8.5z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg>
          <svg class="icon when-open" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M6.4 5 5 6.4l5.6 5.6L5 17.6 6.4 19l5.6-5.6 5.6 5.6 1.4-1.4-5.6-5.6L19 6.4 17.6 5 12 10.6z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg>
        </span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- The browser's own reload, the one control here that works: it plays the run again. -->
  <button class="replay" type="button" data-replay aria-label="Replay the Tolkly preview" title="Replay">
    <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M19.5 12a7.5 7.5 0 1 1-2.2-5.3M19.5 4.5v4.2h-4.2"></path></svg>
  </button>

  <!-- Where it lands: a topic of its own in the team's Telegram group, the bot's card on top. -->
  <div class="tg" aria-hidden="true">
    <div class="tg-head">
      <span class="tg-topic">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M4 6.5A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 6.5 4h11A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 20 6.5v8a2.5 2.5 0 0 1-2.5 2.5H10l-4.2 3.4c-.5.4-1.3 0-1.3-.6V17A2.5 2.5 0 0 1 4 14.5z" fill="currentColor"></path></svg>
      </span>
      <span class="tg-who">
        <b>Can you deliver to a pickup locker? It's for order 48213. · 7f3a</b>
        <span>Shelf support</span>
      </span>
    </div>
    <div class="tg-msg">
      <span class="tg-from">Tolkly</span>
      <p><b>Shelf</b><i class="tsep"></i>Asked for a person</p>
      <p>Order: <code>48213</code></p>
      <p>Page: shelf.example</p>
      <p class="tg-gap"><b>Question</b></p>
      <p class="tg-quote">Can you deliver to a pickup locker? It's for order 48213.</p>
      <p>The AI found no answer in the knowledge base.</p>
      <span class="tg-time">14:02</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<style>
  /*
    The run, on its own clock: plain time from the scene (`data-ease="linear"`)
    turned into seconds, every beat easing on its own. With the scene finished
    — no script, reduced motion — the handoff is what stays on screen: the
    first answer's source and its check at the top of the log, the refusal
    and the operator being brought in under them, the card in the topic.
  */
  .tolkly {
    --s: calc(var(--p) * 10.6);
    /* The launcher arrives with the theme: until the project's colours come,
       the real one stays hidden rather than flash in the default ones. */
    --launch: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 0.2) / 0.3, 1);
    --open: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 0.75) / 0.25, 1);
    /* Typing the two questions, and the moments each is sent. */
    --type1: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 1.05) / 0.9, 1);
    --sent1: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 2) * 40, 1);
    --type2: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 5.85) / 1.35, 1);
    --sent2: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 7.3) * 40, 1);
    /* Something is in the field: from the first key of a question to its send. */
    --full: calc(
      clamp(0, (var(--s) - 1.05) * 40, 1) * (1 - var(--sent1)) + clamp(0, (var(--s) - 5.85) * 40, 1) * (1 - var(--sent2))
    );
    --peek: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 4.95) / 0.3, 1);
    --press: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 9.15) / 0.15, 1);
    --gone: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 9.35) / 0.2, 1);
    --waiting: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 9.4) * 40, 1);
    --tg-t: clamp(0, (var(--s) - 9.85) / 0.5, 1);
    --tg: calc(1 - (1 - var(--tg-t)) * (1 - var(--tg-t)) * (1 - var(--tg-t)));

    position: relative;
    width: 660px;
    height: 700px;
    font-variant-numeric: normal;
  }

  /* ── the browser and the shop in it ─────────────────────────────────── */

  .browser {
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 22px;
    width: 638px;
    height: 664px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    border-radius: 14px;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #fff6f2;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    box-shadow: var(--sh-mock);
  }

  .bar {
    flex: none;
    height: 36px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 0 12px;
    background: #0f1116;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.08);
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #a1a7b3;
  }

  .dots {
    display: flex;
    gap: 7px;
  }

  .dots i {
    width: 10px;
    height: 10px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.11);
  }

  .url {
    flex: 1;
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 6px;
    height: 24px;
    margin-inline: 40px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
  }

  .url svg {
    width: 11px;
    height: 11px;
  }

  .tag {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    height: 22px;
    padding: 0 9px;
    border-radius: 8px;
    border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
    font-size: 11px;
  }

  /* Shelf, as the landing draws it: a warm paper, a brick accent, 12 px corners. */
  .site {
    --s-fg: #2a1712;
    --s-acc: #c8401f;
    position: relative;
    flex: 1;
    padding: 18px 22px;
    font-family: var(--ui);
    color: var(--s-fg);
  }

  .s-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 26px;
    padding-bottom: 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(42, 23, 18, 0.1);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }

  .s-logo {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .s-logo i {
    width: 14px;
    height: 14px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--s-acc);
  }

  .s-nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 18px;
    font-size: 12.5px;
    color: rgba(42, 23, 18, 0.7);
  }

  .s-h {
    width: 260px;
    margin-top: 34px;
    font-size: 27px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.12;
    letter-spacing: -0.01em;
  }

  .s-p {
    margin-top: 12px;
    font-size: 13.5px;
    color: rgba(42, 23, 18, 0.72);
  }

  .s-cta {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    height: 38px;
    margin-top: 18px;
    padding: 0 16px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: var(--s-acc);
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .s-blocks {
    display: flex;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }

  .s-blocks span {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 4px;
    width: 120px;
    flex: none;
    padding: 12px 14px;
    border-radius: 12px;
    background: #fbefe9;
  }

  .s-blocks small {
    font-size: 11.5px;
    color: rgba(42, 23, 18, 0.65);
  }

  .s-blocks b {
    font-size: 17px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* ── the widget, in its own pixels ─────────────────────────────────── */

  /*
    The corner the widget takes, drawn at the product's size and scaled
    down from the bottom right: 1 / 0.85 of the site's height, which leaves
    the window within a few pixels of the 640 the real one stops at.
  */
  .corner {
    /* The site's theme, as the widget reads it: its accent and its text
       colour, its surface, its radius, its font. The rest are the widget's
       own light defaults. */
    --tk-accent: #c8401f;
    --tk-accent-fg: #ffffff;
    --tk-bg: #ffffff;
    --tk-fg: #2a1712;
    --tk-muted: #6f625d;
    --tk-border: #eadcd5;
    --tk-surface: #fbefe9;
    --tk-r: 12px;
    position: absolute;
    right: 0;
    bottom: 0;
    width: 420px;
    height: 741px;
    transform: scale(0.85);
    transform-origin: bottom right;
    font-family: var(--ui);
    color: var(--tk-fg);
  }

  .icon {
    width: 16px;
    height: 16px;
    flex: none;
    fill: none;
    stroke: currentColor;
    stroke-width: 1.75;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }

  .launcher {
    position: absolute;
    right: 20px;
    bottom: 20px;
    width: 56px;
    height: 56px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--tk-accent);
    color: var(--tk-accent-fg);
    box-shadow: 0 8px 24px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.2);
    opacity: var(--launch);
    transform: scale(calc(0.8 + 0.2 * var(--launch)));
  }

  .launcher .icon {
    grid-area: 1 / 1;
    width: 26px;
    height: 26px;
    stroke: none;
  }

  .when-closed {
    opacity: calc(1 - var(--open));
  }

  .when-open {
    opacity: var(--open);
  }

  .window {
    position: absolute;
    right: 20px;
    bottom: 88px;
    top: 20px;
    width: 380px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    background: var(--tk-bg);
    border: 1px solid var(--tk-border);
    border-radius: var(--tk-r);
    box-shadow: 0 24px 64px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.22);
    overflow: hidden;
    opacity: var(--open);
    transform: translateY(calc((1 - var(--open)) * 8px));
  }

  .head {
    flex: none;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 12px;
    padding: 12px 8px 12px 16px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--tk-border);
  }

  .mono {
    width: 36px;
    height: 36px;
    flex: none;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    border-radius: var(--tk-r);
    background: var(--tk-accent);
    color: var(--tk-accent-fg);
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .who {
    flex: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
  }

  .who b {
    font-size: 15px;
    line-height: 20px;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .status-line {
    font-size: 12px;
    line-height: 16px;
    color: var(--tk-muted);
  }

  .x {
    width: 32px;
    height: 32px;
    display: grid;
    place-items: center;
    color: var(--tk-muted);
  }

  .x .icon {
    width: 20px;
    height: 20px;
    stroke: none;
  }

  /*
    A column held to its end: while the messages fit, the filler after them
    takes the rest and they sit at the top; once they do not, there is no
    rest to take and they overflow upwards, off the top of the log.
  */
  .log {
    flex: 1;
    min-height: 0;
    overflow: hidden;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: flex-end;
    padding: 0 16px 12px;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 20px;
  }

  .log::after {
    content: "";
    flex: 1 0 0;
  }

  .log > :first-child {
    margin-top: 16px;
  }

  /*
    A message arriving: it opens its own height, its gap above it included,
    so the ones before it move up by exactly that much. `--h` is a ceiling
    a little over the message's height, `--t` the second it arrives.
  */
  .grow {
